{"name":"Berkshire Lace","hex":"#f0e1cf","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light fabric containing patterns of holes, usually built up from a single thread.","A cord or ribbon passed through eyelets in a shoe or garment, pulled tight and tied to fasten the shoe or garment firmly."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fasten (something) with laces.","To interweave items."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lace"}],"entries":[{"title":"Berkshire","blocks":[{"text":"Berkshire, officially the Royal County of Berkshire, is a ceremonial county in South East England. It is bordered by Oxfordshire to the north, Buckinghamshire to the north-east, Greater London to the east, Surrey to the south-east, Hampshire to the south, and Wiltshire to the west. Reading is the largest settlement and the county town."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Sweep_of_the_Downs_at_Starveall%2C_Berkshire_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4043203.jpg/330px-Sweep_of_the_Downs_at_Starveall%2C_Berkshire_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4043203.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkshire","wikidata":"Q23220"},{"title":"Lace","blocks":[{"text":"Lace is a decorative openwork textile made without the use of pre-existing fabric. Lace can be made by hand or machine. Various techniques can be employed to form lace, each having a distinct category. Lace can also be used to refer to other types of openwork fabric such as cutwork or filet, which use pre-existing fabric."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Verknipte_kantstrook.JPG/330px-Verknipte_kantstrook.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lace","wikidata":"Q231250"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/The_Blade%2C_Abbey_Square%2C_Reading.jp